---
import DocsLayout from "@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro"

const html =
  '<p>This page maps KoAkademy&#39;s capabilities so you know what exists and where to find it. Details for daily work are in the portal guides; configuration details are in the area-specific guides.</p>\n<h2>Core areas</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Area</th>\n<th>What it covers</th>\n<th>Where</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Academic records</td>\n<td>Students, faculty, courses, departments, rooms, senior high strands</td>\n<td>Admin panel</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Classes and scheduling</td>\n<td>Sections, subject assignments, capacity, timetables with conflict detection</td>\n<td>Admin panel and Admin workspace</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Enrollment</td>\n<td>Applications, verification pipeline, class enrollment, reports and analytics</td>\n<td>Admin workspace</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Grading</td>\n<td>Point/percent scales, passing rules, GWA exclusions, finalize and verify workflow</td>\n<td>Admin workspace and Faculty portal</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Finance</td>\n<td>Tuition assessment, cashier payment posting, statements of account, finance reports</td>\n<td>Admin workspace and Cashier module</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Communication</td>\n<td>Announcements with banner display, template-based notifications, e-mail</td>\n<td>Announcement and Notification Center modules</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Reports and exports</td>\n<td>Enrollment reports, student lists, attendance reports (Excel), PDF documents</td>\n<td>Admin panel exporters and downloads</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>PDF documents</td>\n<td>Statements of account, timetables, enrollment assessments</td>\n<td>Generated server-side via Gotenberg</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2>Portals</h2>\n<p>KoAkademy provides three purpose-built workspaces in addition to the Filament administration panel:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Administration panel (<code>/admin</code>)</strong> — records, resources, settings, dashboards, backups, and role management for administrative staff. See the <a href="/docs/user-guide/admin-portal">Admin portal guide</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>Faculty portal</strong> — dashboard, action center, attendance, class posts and submissions, grading, and schedules for teaching staff. See the <a href="/docs/user-guide/faculty-portal">Faculty portal guide</a>.</li>\n<li><strong>Student portal</strong> — classes, schedule, tuition and statements of account, digital ID card, announcements, and notifications for students. See the <a href="/docs/user-guide/student-portal">Student portal guide</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Optional modules</h2>\n<p>Six bundled modules extend the platform: Announcements, Cashier, Inventory,\nLibrary System, Notification Center, and Student Medical Records. Standalone\nComposer modules such as Forms can add further workflows. Each installed module\ncan be enabled or disabled per institution. See the <a href="/docs/user-guide/modules">Modules guide</a>\nand the <a href="/docs/maintainers/module-registry">Module Registry guide</a>.</p>\n<h2>How features are switched</h2>\n<p>KoAkademy has three separate layers of feature control:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Module status</strong> — installed code-level domains enabled or disabled from <strong>Administrators → Marketplace</strong>. The Marketplace does not install Composer packages; a standalone package must already be present in the application image.</li>\n<li><strong>Feature access</strong> — runtime release policy at <code>/administrators/feature-toggles</code>. System administrators manage built-in role defaults, explicit user/role/school targets, named beta groups, percentage rollouts, and scheduled releases. This controls availability, not action permissions or code installation.</li>\n<li><strong>General settings</strong> — institution-wide switches in General Settings, including the student portal, online enrollment, clearances, signature capture, QR codes, and the inventory and library modules.</li>\n</ol>\n<div class="doc-callout doc-callout-note">\n  <p class="doc-callout-label">What this does</p><p>Managed policies take effect on the next request without deleting records or assignments. Existing installations retain legacy feature behavior until an administrator deliberately adopts managed policy. The legacy Filament Features page is read-only.</p>\n</div><h3>Fresh installations and upgrades</h3>\n<p>Fresh installations enable baseline student and faculty functions for their intended roles, including future users. Beta, AI, and developer features are not broadly enabled by default. Public college and TESDA enrollment use installation-wide policy.</p>\n<p>Upgrades start with <strong>Legacy preserved</strong>. Review a feature&#39;s managed impact before adopting it. Existing Pennant rows are not relabeled as confirmed administrator assignments: automatic evaluations and older manual overrides have indistinguishable storage. They remain intact for compatibility rollback.</p>\n<h3>Releasing a feature</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Select the feature and review its built-in role destinations.</li>\n<li>Choose <strong>Built-in role defaults</strong>, <strong>Targets only</strong>, or <strong>Stable percentage</strong>. Targets can allow or deny a user, eligible role, school, or beta group. Deny wins, and targeting cannot grant another role&#39;s feature or action permissions.</li>\n<li>For supported beta features, optionally allow user opt-in. Developer tools remain administrator-controlled.</li>\n<li>Optionally set <strong>Release from</strong> and <strong>Retire at</strong>. Dates display in your browser&#39;s local time and round-trip with explicit offsets. Retirement must follow release; a retirement-only schedule is also supported. No cron task is needed: availability is checked against time on each new request.</li>\n<li>Review impact, then explicitly adopt/save. Impact compares the current state with the draft, counts at most the first 500 eligible users in their primary school, and labels bounded results. Editing the draft invalidates the review. Future schedules and later membership changes can alter access beyond the current-time estimate.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Percentage cohorts are stable per feature, user, and school. Increasing a percentage includes earlier members; lowering it intentionally rolls back that portion of the release. Explicit grants and exclusions remain separate from cohort membership.</p>\n<p>Users outside a managed release receive a dashboard notice when following a page link. Administrator exclusions, wrong-role access, JSON requests, and blocked mutations still return 403; an unavailable write is never disguised as a successful redirect.</p>\n<h3>Rollback</h3>\n<p>Switch a feature back to <strong>Legacy compatibility</strong> to use its preserved legacy results. This does not delete managed policy or targets. Do not purge legacy rows before reviewing that rollback path. Downgrading to an older binary requires separate operator review because older code does not read managed policy.</p>\n<h2>Security and access control</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Roles and permissions</strong> — about 30 built-in roles (from super administrator to registrar, cashier, librarian, professor ranks, and student roles) with per-resource permissions.</li>\n<li><strong>Multi-factor authentication</strong> — TOTP authenticator codes and e-mail codes, plus WebAuthn passkeys for passwordless sign-in.</li>\n<li><strong>Activity logging</strong> — administrative actions are recorded and reviewable under Audit Logs.</li>\n<li><strong>Multi-school context</strong> — staff with access to several schools switch the active school from the organization switcher; records stay scoped to the selected school.</li>\n</ul>\n'
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Platform Features"
  path="/docs/user-guide/features-overview"
  description="A map of what KoAkademy provides, where each capability lives, and how features are switched on or off."
>
  <Fragment set:html={html} />
</DocsLayout>
